WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.357
This is Garth.

2
00:00:01.357 --> 00:00:03.010
Here it is, in two minutes.

3
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.001
Garth is where a team works with a coding agent, in the browser.

4
00:00:08.001 --> 00:00:12.210
Every project is a git repository, shared with the people who work on it.

5
00:00:13.511 --> 00:00:18.324
A project shows what is on main, and what the agent reads: the project's

6
00:00:18.324 --> 00:00:22.870
instructions, its memory and its skills, all kept in the repository.

7
00:00:24.171 --> 00:00:29.443
Start a session, and the agent gets its own sandbox, from a warm pool, on its own

8
00:00:29.443 --> 00:00:29.898
branch.

9
00:00:29.898 --> 00:00:31.395
It is ready in seconds.

10
00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:36.379
Ask for a change in plain words.

11
00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:41.973
The agent reads the code, edits files and runs commands, in this session's sandbox

12
00:00:41.973 --> 00:00:42.314
only.

13
00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:51.393
When it is done, the changes are listed beside the conversation, and the diff is one

14
00:00:51.393 --> 00:00:52.019
click away.

15
00:00:55.319 --> 00:01:00.153
Commit and push from the panel, then merge into main, and the work is there for the

16
00:01:00.153 --> 00:01:00.793
whole team.

17
00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:07.907
A live session can be shared with the project's people, to watch, or to drive it

18
00:01:07.907 --> 00:01:08.392
with you.

19
00:01:09.692 --> 00:01:14.535
Administrators see everyone, and give each person a budget, by the day and by the

20
00:01:14.535 --> 00:01:14.894
month.

21
00:01:16.194 --> 00:01:21.255
Every model call goes through Garth's gateway, so spending is counted as it happens,

22
00:01:21.255 --> 00:01:23.002
by person, project and model.

23
00:01:24.302 --> 00:01:27.800
Sandboxes are fenced by the cluster's network policy.

24
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.487
They reach Garth, and through its proxy only the destinations you list.

25
00:01:32.487 --> 00:01:37.701
Never the cloud's metadata, your private network, the Kubernetes API or another

26
00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:38.229
sandbox.

27
00:01:39.529 --> 00:01:43.431
People sign in with your own identity provider, and you decide who can join.

28
00:01:44.731 --> 00:01:45.821
Garth is free.

29
00:01:45.821 --> 00:01:47.689
Find it at getgarth.com.

30
00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:50.646
Garth is made and owned by Burnspring.

